From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375-motorola-rhodep: expose the GPU's
 remaining speed-bin steps (770 and 840 MHz)

Patch 0007 stopped the GPU OPP table at NOM (650 MHz) and said so:

	Only up to NOM (650 MHz) is exposed for now; the turbo bins
	(770/840/900) can be added once the GPU has been confirmed stable.

It has been stable for a long time, so add them -- but not the three that
comment names, and not from the file it took them from.

Two things were wrong in the original derivation. First, it says the values
came from qcom,gpu-pwrlevels-0 in the vendor blair.dtsi, and blair does
include holi-gpu.dtsi -- but it then does /delete-node/ on
qcom,gpu-pwrlevel-bins and defines four bins of its own, so holi's tables
(which top out at 875) never apply to this SoC at all.

Second, and this is what decides the ceiling, the bin is a fuse, not a
choice. blair declares bins 0, 190, 177 and one more; the first two go to
900 MHz and bin 177 stops at 840. Read the fuse on the device -- qfprom is
at 0x1b40000 and the gpu_speed_bin cell at offset 0x6015, so byte
0x1b46015, which mainline does not expose because sm6375.dtsi has no qfprom
node:

	# python3 mmap of /dev/mem at 0x1b46000, byte 0x15
	gpu_speed_bin = 177

which selects qcom,gpu-pwrlevels-2: 840 (TURBO), 770 (NOM_L1), 650 (NOM),
490, 390, 266. So this part gets 770 and 840, and 900 MHz stays out: it is
listed only for bins 0 and 190 and would be running the GPU past its bin.

The frequencies need nothing from the clock driver -- ftbl_gpu_cc_gx_gfx3d_clk_src
in gpucc-sm6375.c already lists 770, 840 and 900. Only the OPPs were
missing. The corners are translated from the vendor's RPMH levels to the
rpmpd (SMD RPM) ones this SoC actually uses, NOM_L1 -> rpmpd_opp_nom_plus
and TURBO -> rpmpd_opp_turbo, both already defined in sm6375.dtsi, and they
land on VDDGX rather than VDDCX for the reason patch 0007 documents.

Thermal needs no change: the cooling-maps added by patch 0021 use
THERMAL_NO_LIMIT for both bounds, so they pick up the new states on their
own instead of being pinned to the old top index.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375-motorola-rhodep.dts
@@ -1409,10 +1409,21 @@
 		};
 
 		/*
-		 * Frequencies and levels taken from qcom,gpu-pwrlevels-0 in the
-		 * vendor blair.dtsi. Only up to NOM (650 MHz) is exposed for now;
-		 * the turbo bins (770/840/900) can be added once the GPU has been
-		 * confirmed stable.
+		 * Frequencies and levels for this part's speed bin, read from the
+		 * hardware rather than assumed: the fuse at qfprom 0x6015 reads
+		 * 177, which is qcom,gpu-pwrlevels-2 in the vendor blair.dtsi --
+		 * 840 (TURBO) down to 266 (LOW_SVS).
+		 *
+		 * 900 MHz (TURBO_L1) is deliberately absent. It exists only in
+		 * bins 0 and 190, and this part is neither, so exposing it would
+		 * run the GPU past what the silicon was binned for. Note that
+		 * blair replaces holi's tables wholesale (/delete-node/ on
+		 * qcom,gpu-pwrlevel-bins), so holi-gpu.dtsi is the wrong file to
+		 * read for this SoC.
+		 *
+		 * The corners are rpmpd (SMD RPM) levels, not the RPMH ones the
+		 * vendor writes, and they land on VDDGX -- see the comment on
+		 * power-domains above.
 		 */
 		gpu_opp_table: opp-table {
 			compatible = "operating-points-v2";
@@ -1436,6 +1447,16 @@
 				opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <650000000>;
 				required-opps = <&rpmpd_opp_nom>;
 			};
+
+			opp-770000000 {
+				opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <770000000>;
+				required-opps = <&rpmpd_opp_nom_plus>;
+			};
+
+			opp-840000000 {
+				opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <840000000>;
+				required-opps = <&rpmpd_opp_turbo>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 
